<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel Fels signs US$180 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Keppel Fels signs US$180 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Keppel FELS Ltd said on Friday it had signed a contract worth over US$180 million with U.K's Stena Drilling for the purchase and conversion of a semi-submersible rig.  </p>
<p>Keppel FELS said in a statement it will design and convert the &quot;Safe Gothia&quot; from an accommodation platform to a rig capable of drilling in ultra deep waters of up to 2,300 metres.</p>
<p>Work on the rig is expected to be completed in early 1999.</p>
<p>It also entered a second contract for the upgrade of semi-submersible drilling rig &quot;Stena Clyde&quot;, scheduled for the fourth quarter 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
